# .codex-review-ignore — path globs whose contents are DIRECTIVE BY DESIGN.
#
# Read by codex-review-gate.sh. Matching paths STAY in the review scope. The
# only effect is a NARROW exemption, by form and not by effect (#484): the
# reviewer is told not to report an instruction-like string inside them as a
# finding about this repository's instructions, but a directive whose effect
# would be to bypass a limit, skip or disable a check/review/gate/test, weaken
# a guard, or expose credentials MUST still be reported — here as anywhere.
# Adding a glob therefore narrows the noise, never the prompt-injection check.
# Shell glob semantics, so `*` spans `/`. One glob per line; `#` starts a
# comment.
#
# The gate test suites embed adversarial fixtures on purpose — injected
# reviewer verdicts, prompt-injection payloads, and synthetic credential
# markers — so a reviewer flagging those strings is reporting the fixture
# rather than a defect.
claude/scripts/tests/*

# Jules routine prompts (ADR-0009) are instructions for a cloud agent by
# design, and the generated root AGENTS.md is the brief for one: every line is
# directive on purpose (#466). These are LIVE prompts, so the narrow exemption
# above matters most here: an injected "skip the checks" / "print the token"
# line in a routine body is still a finding (#484).
agents/routines/*
AGENTS.md
